~ start
if State.talked_ezra
	Ezra: Don't say I didn't warn ya.
else
	Ezra: Keep back, stranger! Unless you're another one o' them green-glowing phantoms come to suck the marrow outta my bones! In which case... I got a bucket o' rock salt and a rusty shovel waitin' for ya!
	Shayn: I'm not a phantom. I'm human, and I don't want any trouble. 
	Shayn: Name's Shayn. I'm looking for a doctor. Think his name was Silas Hollister. Is he here?
	Ezra: Silas? Old "Crank"? You're a day late and a dollar short, kid. He hitched his covered wagon and headed further up the drag toward the saloon days ago… Before the town went completely to hell.
	Shayn: Did he have the Chrono-Caduceus with him? The healing device?
	Ezra: I don't know what high-falutin' words you're throwin' around, but he had a whole mess o' copper wire and clockwork gear in the back. 
	Ezra: But you ain't gonna make it two blocks down the Dustfall Strip with them feral specters swarming the road, not to mention Marshal Stone shootin' at anything that blinks sideways.
	Shayn: I can take care of myself. Just point me toward the saloon.
	Ezra: Straight down the main street. But if you're gonna survive the walk, you'd better be prepared. Here, take some grease for yer weapon there. I picked it off a scrap wagon.
	Shayn: Thanks…?
	Ezra: And don't say I didn't warn ya; now get off my darn porch.
	$> State.talked_ezra = true

=> END



